{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Read the retained receipt of experiment 03d8630fd2a64384a825524b28696d36-experiment (CheckRun f418b9d6ab8841faa9ab6c35ce1fcd75): setup event 6 shows the restarted node's live configuration empty (log-recorded configuration holds one voter, derived quorum size 1) and result event 7 shows that node granting both RequestVote and RequestPreVote to a candidate absent from its configuration. The child question therefore moves to a witnessed violation, with the receipt recorded as a behavior entry. The next judgment-changing step registered here is the safety consequence of a stale (rather than empty) configuration: whether a restarted node commits with a quorum that is not a majority of the configuration in force, so that an acknowledged write can be superseded.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n  {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@k-empty-admission\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\":\\\"A node whose configuration is empty after a RestoreCommittedLogs restart still answers RequestVote and RequestPreVote with Granted=true for a candidate that appears in no configuration, because both handlers apply their membership rejection only when the candidate's own Servers list is non-empty; the node also adopts the requester's higher term and derives a quorum size of 1 from the empty voter list.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"RestoreCommittedLogs=true with a commit-tracking store; the node restarts with no snapshot so its configuration is empty after NewRaft; the requester's term is higher and its last log entry is at least as recent as the node's; the request is delivered over the transport.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-runfollower-gate\\\",\\\"s-commit-tracking-contract\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"f418b9d6ab8841faa9ab6c35ce1fcd75\\\":[6,7]}}\n ],\n \\\"investigations\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"7e10640e7212486b94a80f04b69febc2-question-1\\\",\n   \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Whether the empty configuration also changes the node's own participation (runFollower election gating) and whether the node accepts AppendEntries from the requester as its leader, both measured rather than derived.\\\"},\n  {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@stale-config-quorum\\\",\\\"parent_id\\\":\\\"680bc27c9c50448a8b63097d98091061-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"question\\\":\\\"Does a node restarted with a stale (smaller) configuration after a RestoreCommittedLogs restart commit entries with a quorum that is not a majority of the configuration in force, so that a write acknowledged to a client can be superseded by a leader elected from the true configuration?\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-scan\\\",\\\"s-restore-committed\\\",\\\"s-runfollower-gate\\\",\\\"s-commit-tracking-contract\\\"],\n   \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"r.configurations.latest, commitment.setConfiguration and quorumSize() all use the recovered configuration, so a stale restarted node can win an election against the stale voter set and commit an entry with acknowledgements from fewer than a majority of the true configuration; those holders can then be removed from service while a true majority elects a leader whose log lacks the entry.\\\",\n   \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Build a five-voter cluster whose commit-tracking stores are retained, take a snapshot on one follower while the configuration is still the three-voter set, commit the configuration change that adds the other two voters plus later commands on that follower, restart it (stale configuration), remove the serving leader and the two voters not in the stale set so that the stale quorum is reachable, apply a write and record its future result, then remove the stale leader and its acknowledgement partner, restart the remaining voters and record whether the new leader's log and FSM contain the acknowledged write.\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"7e10640e7212486b94a80f04b69febc2-question-1\\\",\n   \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"03d8630fd2a64384a825524b28696d36-experiment\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-runfollower-gate\\\",\\\"s-commit-tracking-contract\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"f418b9d6ab8841faa9ab6c35ce1fcd75\\\":[6,7]},\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Current account: the empty configuration produced by a RestoreCommittedLogs restart removes the membership admission check from vote and pre-vote handling, and the retained execution shows the resulting admission of a non-member. Parsed event 6 (setup): live_config_after_restart is empty with live_voters 0 and derived_quorum_size 1, while log_recorded_config still holds the one bootstrapped voter, so the configuration in force (recorded in the node's own log) is not what the node uses. Parsed event 7 (result, same node and configuration): request_vote_granted=true with request_vote_term 3, request_prevote_granted=true with request_prevote_term 4, candidate_in_live_config=false, node_term_after_requests 3 - that is, a candidate appearing in no configuration was granted a vote and a pre-vote, and the node adopted the requester's higher term. Both declared comparisons are violated at index 7. Mechanism from source: requestVote and requestPreVote reject candidates outside the configuration only when the handler's own Servers list is non-empty, a leniency documented for the bootstrap case, so an empty list accepts any candidate; quorumSize() over the empty voter list yields 1. Consequence boundaries: the requester's log was made at least as recent as the node's, so no recency rule applied, and the restarted node has no known leader after its own recovery, so the leader-availability rejection did not apply either; the node's own election gating (runFollower aborting when no peers are known) is source-derived, not measured, and is left as the next discriminator.\\\",\n   \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n    \\\"Granting a vote when the configuration is empty is intentional behaviour for a cluster that is being bootstrapped; the defect here is that the node's own recovery path leaves the configuration empty in a cluster that is not being bootstrapped, not the leniency itself.\\\",\n    \\\"The probe supplied a candidate whose log was at least as recent as the node's and whose term was higher, which is what makes the vote grant observable; a stale or older candidate would still be rejected by the log-recency rules.\\\",\n    \\\"The same configuration gap is repaired by any later configuration entry or installed snapshot, so a healthy cluster with continuing traffic repairs the node without operator action.\\\"],\n   \\\"limitations\\\":[\n    \\\"Measured on a single-node in-memory cluster with snapshotting disabled and the repository's InmemCommitTrackingStore, with the candidate reaching the node through the in-memory transport.\\\",\n    \\\"Only RequestVote and RequestPreVote admission was driven; whether the node accepts AppendEntries or accepts leadership from a non-member, and whether its own candidacy is suppressed, is not measured here.\\\",\n    \\\"The node adopted the requester's term, but no consequence of that term change (for example disruption of an existing leader) was measured.\\\"]}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
